diff --git a/Extension/CustomModes/README.md b/Extension/CustomModes/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7932884
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Extension/CustomModes/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,97 @@
+# Custom multiplayer modes
+
+ReSkate's own game modes on the pause menu's **Multiplayer** page: each mode gets a tab of its own there, after the page's own tabs (SERVER BROWSER, HOST LOBBY, ...). The page is otherwise unchanged. Offline, where the Multiplayer page is normally left out, it shows with just the modes' tabs (a mode can be played alone).
+
+- **Its tabs:** one per mode, in the order they registered.
+- **Left side**, for the chosen mode: its own panel, with settings, status and buttons.
+- **Right side:** **PLAY ONLINE**. Host a game for the mode, or join a game that plays it.
+
+Modes run on the players' games. Lobbies and dedicated servers only advertise which mode they're for.
+
+## What a mode provides
+
+A mode registers once at startup with `custom_modes::add` (`custom_modes.h`). The menu does the rest.
+
+```cpp
+#include "Extension/CustomModes/custom_modes.h"
+
+custom_modes::add({
+    .id = "domination",                 // 1-16 of a-z 0-9 -: what lobbies and servers advertise
+    .name = "Domination",
+    .tagline = "Own the most spots",
+    .panel = [] {                       // client thread, a few times a second while the menu is open
+        custom_modes::Panel p;
+        p.description = "Own the most spots in the park.";
+        p.map = "levels/game/...";      // where it is played ("" any map); hosting loads it first
+        p.map_name = "Red-bowl park";
+        p.map_here = /* the player is on it */ true;
+        p.settings.push_back({"Round length", "5:00", "", "mymode set duration 240", "mymode set duration 360"});
+        p.buttons.push_back({"Start round", "", "mymode start"});
+        return p;
+    },
+    .joined = [] { /* the player joined a game advertised for this mode */ },
+});
+```
+
+**Panel fields:**
+- **Settings:** each row is a label and value. Pressing it runs `press`; adjusting it left or right runs `less` / `more`. All three are console commands of the mode's own.
+- **Status lines** are shown and not pressable: the round going on, the standings.
+- **Dropdowns:** a setting with `choices` is a dropdown. Pressed, it lists them under it, one full-width row each, and picking one runs its console command.
+- **Map:** `map` (a `load` destination) and `map_name` show where the mode is played. `map_choices` make the row a dropdown, for a mode played on several maps. A `map_name` with no `map` names a map that can't be loaded here.
+- **Buttons** run their `command`. A button whose command contains ` start`, pressed on another map, loads the mode's map first.
+- **`available` / `unavailable`** says whether the mode can be played here, and why not.
+
+## Hosting a game for a mode
+
+The menu's **Host a <mode> game**, or the console's `modes host <id> [public|code] [players] [name]`:
+1. loads the mode's map if the player isn't on it;
+2. waits for it, giving up after 4 minutes;
+3. hosts with the player's saved tick rate and lobby name;
+4. makes the lobby advertise the mode (`multiplayer::set_advertised_mode`, published as the Steam lobby value `rs_mode`).
+
+Other commands:
+- `modes cancel` stops waiting.
+- `modes status` says what hosting is doing.
+- Hosting already? The menu offers **Advertise your game as <mode>**.
+
+When the session ends, nothing is advertised anymore.
+
+A **dedicated server** is for a mode through its config: `[server] mode = "domination"`. It's advertised in the browser tags as `g<id>`. The server doesn't run the mode; the players' games do.
+
+## Finding games
+
+The menu lists the browser's lobbies and servers whose advertised mode is the chosen one (`MultiplayerLobby::mode`), and joins one when pressed. **Find <mode> games** refreshes the browser's lists.
+
+When the player joins a game from the browser, its mode's `joined` is called once. Domination uses this to join the round going on.
+
+Games joined by code carry no mode. The mode's own messages still reach those players.
+
+## Compatibility
+
+- **Older clients** ignore `rs_mode` and the `g` tag, so they still list and join these games.
+- **Mode ids** that aren't valid are dropped; an empty id means no mode. The rule is `valid_mode_id` in `Engine/Game/Multiplayer/session_model.h`.
+- **Tag budget:** the `g` tag takes up to 18 bytes of a server's 127-byte tag budget, out of the space the server name would otherwise use.
+- **Offline mode:** the Multiplayer page shows with only the modes' tabs, and their online part says "Multiplayer is off in offline mode". The modes' own panels still work, for example a solo round.
+
+## Files
+
+| File | What it holds |
+|---|---|
+| `custom_modes.h/.cpp` | The registry, hosting for a mode, `joined`, the advertised mode |
+| `custom_modes_commands.cpp` | The `modes` console commands |
+| `Extension/UI/NativeMenu/native_menu.cpp` | The Multiplayer tab shown offline too when a mode is installed (`custom_modes::count()`) |
+| `Extension/UI/Overlay/hub_page.cpp` (`modes_page`) | A tab per mode on the Multiplayer page, after its own: the mode's panel, PLAY ONLINE. Tabs shrink to fit when there are more than the page is wide |
+| `Extension/UI/Overlay/overlay.h` (`CustomModesModel`) | The modes' model, filled in `Runtime/client_tick.cpp` |
+| `Extension/Multiplayer/Steam/steam_lobbies.*` | `set_mode`, and `rs_mode` published and read |
+| `Server/steam_server.*`, `Extension/Multiplayer/Steam/steam_server_browser.cpp` | The `g` tag |
+| `Server/server_config.*` | The server's `mode` setting |
+| `Extension/Multiplayer/Session/session.*` | `set_advertised_mode` / `advertised_mode` |
+
+## Tests
+
+Build with `-DDINGOSDK_BUILD_MULTIPLAYER_TESTS=ON`, then run `ctest -R "multiplayer_protocol|multiplayer_lobbies"`. They check:
+- a server's mode round-trips through its tags, and invalid modes are dropped;
+- lobby `rs_mode` values are read, and a missing or invalid one reads as none without refusing the lobby;
+- the id rule.
+
+That option also builds two music probe tools that fail to link in this tree. They're unrelated to this change; build the two test targets on their own.
diff --git a/Extension/CustomModes/custom_modes.cpp b/Extension/CustomModes/custom_modes.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c24bc63
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Extension/CustomModes/custom_modes.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,187 @@
+#include "custom_modes.h"
+#include "Engine/Core/Log/logging.h"
+#include "Engine/Core/Platform/launcher_support.h"
+#include "Extension/Multiplayer/Session/session.h"
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <chrono>
+#include <format>
+#include <mutex>
+#include <optional>
+
+namespace dingosdk::custom_modes {
+namespace {
+using Clock = std::chrono::steady_clock;
+constexpr auto host_patience = std::chrono::minutes(4);
+
+struct PendingHost {
+    std::string mode, name;
+    bool public_lobby{};
+    unsigned capacity{};
+    Clock::time_point asked;
+};
+struct State {
+    std::mutex mutex;
+    std::vector<Mode> modes;
+    std::optional<PendingHost> pending;
+    std::string status;
+    std::string advertising;        // the mode this player's hosted game advertises
+    std::uint64_t handled_lobby{};  // the joined game whose mode was told `joined` already
+};
+State &state() {
+    static auto *value = new State;
+    return *value;
+}
+void say(logging::Level level, const std::string &text) { logging::write(level, logging::Channel::runtime, "Custom modes: " + text); }
+
+const Mode *find(const State &s, std::string_view id) {
+    for (const auto &mode : s.modes)
+        if (mode.id == id) return &mode;
+    return nullptr;
+}
+Panel panel_of(const Mode &mode) {
+    try {
+        return mode.panel();
+    } catch (const std::exception &error) {
+        Panel panel;
+        panel.available = false;
+        panel.unavailable = std::string("This mode could not show its panel: ") + error.what();
+        return panel;
+    }
+}
+} // namespace
+
+bool add(Mode mode) noexcept {
+    try {
+        if (!valid_mode_id(mode.id) || mode.name.empty() || !mode.panel) return false;
+        auto &s = state();
+        std::lock_guard lock(s.mutex);
+        if (find(s, mode.id)) return false;
+        s.modes.push_back(std::move(mode));
+        return true;
+    } catch (...) {
+        return false;
+    }
+}
+
+std::size_t count() noexcept {
+    auto &s = state();
+    std::lock_guard lock(s.mutex);
+    return s.modes.size();
+}
+
+std::vector<Listed> list() {
+    std::vector<Mode> modes;
+    {
+        auto &s = state();
+        std::lock_guard lock(s.mutex);
+        modes = s.modes; // panels are asked for outside the lock: a mode may take its own
+    }
+    std::vector<Listed> result;
+    for (const auto &mode : modes) result.push_back({mode.id, mode.name, mode.tagline, panel_of(mode)});
+    return result;
+}
+
+std::string host(std::string_view id, bool public_lobby, unsigned capacity, std::string_view name) {
+    auto &s = state();
+    std::unique_lock lock(s.mutex);
+    // (A refusal is also the hosting status, so the menu that asked says why.)
+    const auto refuse = [&](std::string why) {
+        s.status = why;
+        return "error: " + why;
+    };
+    const auto *mode = find(s, id);
+    if (!mode) return refuse("No custom mode " + std::string(id) + " (modes list shows them).");
+    if (launcher::offline_mode()) return refuse("Multiplayer is off in offline mode.");
+    const auto m = multiplayer::model();
+    if (m.active && !m.hosting) return refuse("You are in someone else's game; leave it first.");
+    if (m.active && m.hosting) {
+        // Already hosting: the game advertises this mode from now on.
+        s.advertising = mode->id;
+        multiplayer::set_advertised_mode(mode->id);
+        s.status = "Your game now advertises " + mode->name + ".";
+        return s.status;
+    }
+    capacity = std::clamp(capacity, 2u, static_cast<unsigned>(multiplayer_lobby_player_limit));
+    s.pending = PendingHost{mode->id, std::string(name), public_lobby, capacity, Clock::now()};
+    const auto mode_copy = *mode;
+    lock.unlock();
+    const auto panel = panel_of(mode_copy);
+    lock.lock();
+    s.status = panel.map.empty() || panel.map_here ? "Hosting a " + mode_copy.name + " game..."
+                                                   : "Hosting a " + mode_copy.name + " game once " + panel.map_name + " has loaded...";
+    say(logging::Level::info, s.status);
+    return s.status + (panel.map.empty() || panel.map_here ? "" : " (load " + panel.map + ")");
+}
+
+std::string cancel_host() {
+    auto &s = state();
+    std::lock_guard lock(s.mutex);
+    if (!s.pending) return "Nothing is waiting to be hosted.";
+    s.pending.reset();
+    s.status = "Hosting cancelled.";
+    return s.status;
+}
+
+HostState host_state() {
+    auto &s = state();
+    std::lock_guard lock(s.mutex);
+    return {s.pending ? s.pending->mode : s.advertising, s.status, s.pending.has_value()};
+}
+
+void tick() noexcept {
+    try {
+        auto &s = state();
+        std::unique_lock lock(s.mutex);
+        if (s.modes.empty()) return;
+        const auto m = multiplayer::model();
+        // A game was hosted for a mode: once the session is over, nothing is advertised.
+        if (!m.active && !s.advertising.empty() && !s.pending) {
+            s.advertising.clear();
+            multiplayer::set_advertised_mode({});
+        }
+        if (!m.active) s.handled_lobby = 0;
+        // Waiting to host: once the mode's map is in and the player is in game.
+        if (s.pending) {
+            auto pending = *s.pending;
+            const auto *mode = find(s, pending.mode);
+            if (!mode || Clock::now() - pending.asked > host_patience) {
+                s.pending.reset();
+                s.status = "Hosting gave up: the map did not load in time.";
+                return;
+            }
+            const auto mode_copy = *mode;
+            lock.unlock();
+            const auto panel = panel_of(mode_copy);
+            const bool ready = (panel.map.empty() || panel.map_here) && m.local_ready && !m.active;
+            if (!ready) return;
+            const auto tps = m.saved_host.tps ? m.saved_host.tps : 30u;
+            const auto name = !pending.name.empty() ? pending.name
+                            : !m.saved_host.lobby_name.empty() ? m.saved_host.lobby_name : mode_copy.name + " game";
+            multiplayer::set_advertised_mode(mode_copy.id);
+            const bool queued = multiplayer::queue_command(
+                "host-config", std::format("{} {} {} {}", pending.public_lobby ? "public" : "code", pending.capacity, tps, name), {});
+            lock.lock();
+            s.pending.reset();
+            s.advertising = queued ? mode_copy.id : std::string();
+            s.status = queued ? (pending.public_lobby ? "Hosting a public " : "Hosting a join-code ") + mode_copy.name + " game."
+                              : "Hosting failed: the multiplayer queue is busy; try again.";
+            say(logging::Level::info, s.status);
+            return;
+        }
+        // Joined a game advertised for a mode: tell the mode, once.
+        if (m.active && !m.hosting && m.connected && m.public_lobby && m.public_lobby != s.handled_lobby) {
+            const auto row = std::ranges::find_if(m.lobbies, [&](const MultiplayerLobby &lobby) { return lobby.id == m.public_lobby; });
+            if (row == m.lobbies.end()) return;
+            s.handled_lobby = m.public_lobby;
+            if (const auto *mode = find(s, row->mode); mode && mode->joined) {
+                const auto joined = mode->joined;
+                const auto name = mode->name;
+                lock.unlock();
+                say(logging::Level::info, "joined a " + name + " game");
+                joined();
+            }
+        }
+    } catch (...) {
+    }
+}
+}
diff --git a/Extension/CustomModes/custom_modes.h b/Extension/CustomModes/custom_modes.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d44132b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Extension/CustomModes/custom_modes.h
@@ -0,0 +1,93 @@
+#pragma once
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <functional>
+#include <string>
+#include <string_view>
+#include <vector>
+
+// Custom multiplayer modes: ReSkate's own game modes (Domination, ...), each a tab of its own on
+// the pause menu's Multiplayer page, after the page's own tabs (hub_page.cpp modes_page). A mode
+// registers itself once with add(); the page then shows its panel, hosts games for it and finds
+// games that play it. Offline, the Multiplayer page is there for the modes alone (played alone).
+// README.md shows how a mode plugs in.
+//
+// - A mode's panel is plain data: settings, status lines and buttons, each pressed one running a
+//   console command of the mode's own. The menu draws every mode the same way.
+// - Hosting: a public lobby or a join-code session advertising the mode (the lobby's rs_mode; a
+//   dedicated server's `mode` setting). The mode's map is loaded first if the mode names one.
+// - Finding: the browser's lobbies and servers whose advertised mode is this one.
+// - Joining a game advertised for a mode calls the mode's `joined`, once.
+// Modes run on the players' games; servers only advertise them.
+namespace dingosdk::custom_modes {
+// One entry of a dropdown: picking it runs its console command.
+struct Choice {
+    std::string label, command;
+    std::string note;   // on its right: "not downloaded", "12 spots", ...
+    bool chosen = false; // the one in use now
+};
+struct Setting {
+    std::string label, value;
+    std::string press;      // console command run when the row is pressed ("" none)
+    std::string less, more; // console commands for a row adjusted left / right ("" none: a plain row)
+    bool enabled = true;
+    std::vector<Choice> choices; // non-empty: a dropdown (pressing the row lists them under it)
+};
+struct Line {
+    std::string label, value;
+};
+struct Button {
+    std::string label, value, command; // `command`: the console command it runs
+    bool enabled = true;
+};
+struct Panel {
+    std::string description;          // a sentence or two: what the mode is
+    bool available = true;            // playable here and now
+    std::string unavailable;          // why not, when it is not
+    std::string map_name, map;        // where it is played (a `load` destination); empty: any map
+    bool map_here = true;             // the local player is on that map
+    // A mode played on several maps: the Map row is a dropdown of them (empty: it only shows the map).
+    // `map_name` alone (no `map`) names a map that can't be loaded here.
+    std::vector<Choice> map_choices;
+    std::vector<Setting> settings;    // the next round's settings
+    std::vector<Line> status;         // the round going on: time left, standings, ...
+    std::vector<Button> buttons;      // start, join, stop, ...
+    std::string note;                 // a line under the panel
+};
+struct Mode {
+    std::string id;      // what lobbies and servers advertise: 1 to 16 of a-z, 0-9 and '-'
+    std::string name;    // "Domination"
+    std::string tagline; // "Own the most spots"
+    // The panel as it is now. Called on the client thread a few times a second while the menu
+    // is open, so it must be quick and must not block.
+    std::function<Panel()> panel;
+    // Optional: the local player has just joined a game advertised for this mode (client thread).
+    std::function<void()> joined;
+};
+// Registers a mode (startup, any thread). False for an invalid id, no panel, or an id taken.
+bool add(Mode mode) noexcept;
+
+struct Listed {
+    std::string id, name, tagline;
+    Panel panel;
+};
+// Every registered mode in the order they were added, each with its panel now (client thread).
+std::vector<Listed> list();
+// How many modes are registered (any thread; no panels asked for).
+std::size_t count() noexcept;
+
+// Hosts a game for a mode: a public lobby (or join code) advertising it, with `capacity` players
+// and an optional lobby name. When the mode names a map the local player is not on, the game is
+// hosted once that map has loaded (load it first: the menu does). Any thread.
+std::string host(std::string_view id, bool public_lobby, unsigned capacity, std::string_view name = {});
+std::string cancel_host();
+struct HostState {
+    std::string mode;   // the mode the game being hosted (or waited for) advertises
+    std::string status; // what hosting is doing
+    bool pending = false;
+};
+HostState host_state();
+
